  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "They never led and still almost stole it.",
    "what_this_means": "Luis Garc\u00eda Jr. drove in two with a home run in the eighth, cutting it to 3\u20134, but that was the only run they could squeeze from eleven runners in scoring position. Weathers lasted just 3.1 innings, forcing the bullpen into a grind. Yerry De los Santos held two scoreless before the damage was done. The math is simple: one conversion on eleven RISP chances is not winning baseball, not in a division three games back where every loss tightens the margin. They had the window. They didn't open it wide enough.",
    "what_to_watch": "This is a team chasing in its own house and coming up one swing short. Garc\u00eda's moment mattered. It kept the scoreboard honest late. But the game was decided by the silent innings before it, by the runners left standing in the first and second and ninth. The bullpen did what it could with an early exit, but a short outing by the starter demands an offensive answer, and the lineup delivered only once when it had eleven chances. Fragility is how you lose three straight one-run games in a week.",
